description=Small fixes and finishing touches for vanilla. Reading for pleasure is overhauled: every novel, comic, magazine and newspaper has a genre, a real page count and a hidden quality; a read takes hours, not minutes, its relief arrives page by page, and a book you put down is bookmarked (right-click for "Read a chapter"). Each character likes one genre and dislikes another, found out by reading. Finishing a book gives the Good Read moodle for a day or two with a small bonus matched to the genre, real 1993 books turn up in loot alongside the game's own, and Fast Reader finishes more of them. Its own sandbox page, one switch turns it off; skill books and recipe magazines are untouched. Cold packs and coolers work: chill a cold pack in a fridge (half way) or a freezer (fully), or leave it out below freezing, then put it in a cooler. The cooler keeps food as cold as a fridge does, about 6 hours for each frozen pack (a sandbox setting), and the packs and the cooler show how cold they are in their names. A Collection button on the sidebar opens a checklist for each character of the skill books, recipe magazines, VHS tapes, CDs, key rings, mementos and tools they own: tick what you have, and those items say so in their tooltip and are set Unwanted, so they grey out and Take All leaves them. Right-click a washing machine to put every dirty or bloody garment you carry into it in one go. Also, when Item Rarity UI is active, modded items get a rarity colour worked out from the loot lists the same way Item Rarity UI does it for vanilla. With This Is Your Life, finished books go in the survivor journal. Singleplayer only for now.
